    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "radius",
     "diameter",
     "compass"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A circle is the set of points at the same distance from the centre. That distance is the radius. The diameter is twice the radius and passes through the centre.\nTo draw a circle, set the compass to the radius, put the point at the centre and turn.\nTo copy a line segment, set the compass to its length and mark the same length with an arc."
    }
